  "caption": [
    {
      "text": "NuExpansionHunter v1.1.0 versus stock ExpansionHunter v5.0.0 · GangSTR hg38 v13 (832,152 loci) · 64 completed whole-genome pairs across 23 genomes on AMD EPYC 9634 nodes with 188 GB RAM. Each pair used the same node, BAM, thread count and pinned CPUs. "
    },
    {
      "text": "v1.1.0 benchmark report",
      "url": "https://github.com/BioCode-Commons/NuExpansionHunter/blob/51748b123d5cc8cd2191787e49657289c2b2ef59/docs/08_Benchmark.md"
    }
  ],
  "note": [
    {
      "text": "Geometric mean speedups were 9.77× at 4 threads (8 pairs), 10.18× at 8 (21 pairs), and 11.02× at 16 (23 pairs). At 32 threads, stock v5.0.0 hit the 172 GiB memory cap on 9 of 21 genomes. NuExpansionHunter was 19.02× faster on the 12 completed pairs and 9.7–10.5× faster on five genomes against v5.0.0 rebuilt with jemalloc and libdeflate. All 64 completed pairs matched the VCF, JSON, BAM header, and decoded BAM record multiset."
    }
  ],
